    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain email blocklist as a new OfficeFloor function-injection step, following the project's endpoint conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerEmailDomain.java` \u2014 a `Validate`-style step that reads the (already normalized/lower-cased) email via `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, extracts the domain, and throws when it's in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Absent/blank email is left untouched (email stays optional).\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainException.java` \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`).\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400` with `OwnerValidationErrors([\"email\"])`, matching the existing `InvalidOwnerEmail` handler's shape.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...DisposableEmailDomainException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- Added an `emailDomain` step immediately after `normalizeEmail` in both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (the PUT step carries `govern: [ transaction ]` to match its pipeline), so the check runs on the normalized email for both create and update.\n\nThe new acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (POST with `x@mailinator.com` \u2192 400) passes, and the full build is green.",
